Track 1: A Highway Cantina Spans the Buffer Zone
- Story & Context: Outside the crumbling toll plazas of Kustrin-Kietz, Vance bypassed a series of municipal sensor loops to turn the entire four-lane bridge into a giant, low-frequency transducer. Local commuters stranded in night-shift blockades watched in disbelief as their car frames began to vibrate to a hypnotic, 124 BPM metallic pulse. By midnight, hundreds of drivers had cut their engines to listen as a ghost-like horn section drifted over the black water, marking the moment protest turned into a subcultural religion. "The road forgets where your tires have been, but the steel remembers the weight," whispered the broadcast over the hijacked traffic radio frequency.
